# fstack messages to the human

If this workspace has no `fstack.yaml`, ignore this rule.

Every bot-to-human message goes through the `tldr` skill before it is sent. Question cards, escalations, review requests, release questions, and status reports all use it.

Keep these verbatim, outside the short rewrite: the question id, the options, the recommended default, the impact lines, `release.command`, verified shas, and pull request URLs.

`notify: conversation` delivers in this chat. Any other notify value is an outward message and waits for approval of the exact text.
